  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Sometimes I take my computer with me to places where the wifi connection is much, much slower than at my normal house, and work on vrchat world and avatars from these locations. I'll often make several uploads, and while Im fine with having to reupload the entire world to vrchat's servers, having to then re-download the world that locally exists on my machine when I enter vrchat client next is really frustrating, and the same goes for avatars. After a world or avatar gets packaged and uploaded to vrchat's servers, there should be a button popup in the Unity sdk that asks if you would like that avatar or world to be automatically cached into vrchat's files. that would make updating avatars and worlds so much quicker on slow wifi and internet connections because avatars and worlds wouldn't need to be uploaded and then re-downloaded every time an update was made, because the creator would just have it auto-cached on their system.",
